    {
      "text": "On the Gram determinants of the Specht modules — For every partition λ of a positive integer n, let Sλ be the corresponding Specht module of the symmetric group Sn, and let det(λ) ∈Z denote the Gram\n\n**On the Gram determinants of the Specht modules**\n\n*Linda Hoyer*\n\n19 pp, 4 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** For every partition λ of a positive integer n, let Sλ be the corresponding Specht module of the symmetric group Sn, and let det(λ) ∈Z denote the Gram determinant of the canonical bilinear form with respect to the standard basis of Sλ. Writing det(λ) = m · 2a(2) λ for integers a(2) λ and m with m odd, we show that if the dimension of Sλ is even, then a(2) λ is also even. This confirms a conjecture posed by Richard Parker in the special case of the symmetric groups.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; Introduction; Preliminaries; Proof of Theorem 1.1",
      "lang": "en",
      "state": "draft",
      "drafted_by": {
        "kind": "script",
        "id": "scripts/summarize-library.py"
      },
